    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d124">

                <pb facs="0120" n="106" sameAs="frus:frus1942v06/pg106"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">825.85/133: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Chile</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Bowers</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Santiago</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-07-03T14:00:00-05:00">July 3, 1942—2
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 7:30 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1089. Department’s 753, June 30, 9 p.m.<anchor n="51" xml:id="d124-f1"/> All
                    Chilean vessels under control Government whose approval would have to be
                    obtained before any arrangements could be made. Sub-Secretary Commerce<anchor
                        n="52" xml:id="d124-f2"/> states that to relieve present shortage
                    possibility of allotting additional ships for service between Chile and the
                    United States now under consideration. He promises more specific information
                    about July 9. The ships in question and present trades are as follows: <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Chollin, Federico Schwager</hi> coastwise coal; <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Millabu</hi> Peruvian sugar; <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Castilla</hi> coastwise; <hi rendition="#italic">California</hi> single
                    trip Argentine wheat.</p>
                <p>There appears no possibility obtaining Chilean vessels for service other than to
                    the United States.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bowers</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d124-f1" n="51" xml:id="d124-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed; it inquired whether certain named vessels could be diverted to war
                    shipping.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d124-f2" n="52" xml:id="d124-f2-content">
                <p>Ricardo Heatley.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
